       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily for adults. Going above 10 mg raises the risk of hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema, and it adds little blood-pressure benefit. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nWhich of these do you want?\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, a typical starting dose, to titrate up.\n- **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily as written**, if the dose is intentional. Please confirm, and I can add a note with the rationale.\n- **A different dose or an add-on agent**, such as an ACE inhibitor/ARB or a thiazide, if the blood pressure isn't controlled on the current dose.\n\nTell me which one and I'll enter it right away."
      }
